{"id":"721b37ada69f8804a84d2f25c00be23f0256bcc6aa2adeded48c097df7063fbf","at":"2026-10-27T05:46:41Z","commit":"963a1431394075ffe9fcbe06375bacfbcc51619a","parents":["a9c283ae3f727cec01c29ce63ec3323c45c7c403d14059dce8a9fae5181aa7bf"],"op":"relate","type":"verifies","ends":[{"kind":"test","id":"Macaw.Auth.Ash.BackendTest: sessions in the token resource: a disabled user's session is revoked as :disabled, one past its expiry as :expired, untold","hash":"b4eb27a2"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/02-sessions.md#ash-sessions-idle","hash":"caca94ee"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"a look-up without :touch leaves last_used_at (touch: false the default); touched every 13 days the session never idles but is :expired past its row's expires_at (the JWT's 30 days) and its jti revoked; a disabled user's session is :disabled and revoked; refute_receive shows neither is announced. Not checked: the revocation racing the touch write (no deterministic seam)","basis":"review"}
